he scope of this date scan report\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9e2a1d88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-07-06-Vulnerability-Scan.md\", \"id\": \"b20a1aa0db99edad\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2906889321624709, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08838861737495844, \"vector_similarity\": 0.762723, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-07-06-Vulnerability-Scan.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9e2a1d88a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-07-06-Vulnerability-Scan.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-07-06-Vulnerability-Scan.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 867, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:00:56\", \"token_count\": 370, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-09\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Security Patch - CORS Issue\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-07-10\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-07-15\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-07-10 14:20] Diana**: @Bob, I just ran a security scan on the API. We've got a wide-open CORS policy. `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` is a no-go for this project.\\n\\n**[2026-07-10 14:23] Bob**: Oops, that was left over from local testing on the scaffold. I'll tighten it up now.\\n\\n**[2026-07-10 14:43] Bob**: Applying the CORS patch. It now only allows requests from the defined `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` in the environment config.\\n\\n**[2026-07-10 14:50] Diana**: Scan is coming back clean now.\\n\\n**[2026-07-10 14:52] Bob**: Thanks for the catch, Diana. I've added a lint check to prevent `*` from being committed