hread: Windows Signing Gap\\n\\n**Channel**: #releases\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-09-02\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 09:14] Evan**: Windows Defender and SmartScreen are both flagging the build for pilot testers — unsigned binaries get treated as untrusted by default.\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:13] Alice**: Is the missing code-signing certificate the actual blocker here?\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:14] Evan**: Yes. We still don't have one. Until we do, every pilot install is going to trip a warning at best, get blocked outright at worst.\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:16] Diana**: Release blocker?\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:17] Bob**: Copy.\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:18] Evan**: It stays open as far as I'm concerned — this isn't something we can work around on the engineering side, we need the certificate.\\n\\n**[2026-09-02 10:59] Alice**: Let's keep it open on the release gate rather than pushing it off the board. I'll chase the certificate process.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 37 slack thread window sign gap channel releas date 2026 09 02 2026 09 02 09 14 evan window defend and smartscreen are both flag the build for pilot tester unsign binari get treat a untrust by default 2026 09 02 10 13 alic is the miss code sign certif the actual blocker here 2026 09 02 10 14 evan yes we still don t have one until we do everi pilot instal is go to trip a warn at best get block outright at worst 2026 09 02 10 16 diana releas blocker 2026 09 02 10 17 bob copi 2026 09 02 1018 evan it stay open a far a i m concern this isn t someth we can work around on the engin side we need the certif 2026 09 02 10 59 alic let s keep it open on the releas gate rather than push it off the board i ll chase the certif process\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e911fa1a8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-09-02-windows-signing-gap.md\", \"id\": \"4223f88ffbddf892\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"importa