rtifact out the other end now.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:06] Bob**: Does it actually run, or just build?\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:24] Evan**: Runs. Installed it on a Windows box and it's passing the same sanity checks we run on Linux.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:26] Diana**: Does this mean Windows compatibility is done?\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:36] Evan**: The engineering work for the Windows build is complete — packaging works, the binary is sound. Code-signing is a separate item we haven't even started on yet, so I wouldn't call the whole thing closed.\\n\\n**[2026-08-12 09:45] Alice**: Understood, we'll track signing on its own. Good progress on the build itself.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 38 slack thread window build artifact channel releas date 2026 08 12 2026 08 12 09 05 evan path fix unblock the window packag attempt i ve got a build artifact out the other end now 2026 08 12 09 06 bob doe it actual run or just build 2026 08 12 09 24 evan run instal it on a window box and it s pass the same saniti check we run on linux 2026 08 12 09 26 diana doe this mean window compat is done 2026 08 12 09 36 evan the engin work for the window build is complet packag work the binari is sound code sign is a separ item we haven t even start on yet so i wouldn t call the whole thing close 2026 08 12 09 45 alic understood we ll track sign on it own good progress on the build itself\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8e7f9688a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-windows-build-artifact.md\", \"id\": \"61bccaf0a0dfface\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.30116545666654837, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.09444852666649768, \"vector_similarity\": 0.78350496, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-windows-build-artifact.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8e7f9688a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-windows-build-artifact.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-12-windows-build-artifact.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 859, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:30\", \"token_count\": 268, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-36\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Windows Path Handling\\n\\n**Channel**: #releases\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-10\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 10:19] Evan**: Windows builds have been failing on path separators — the ingestion logic has backslash assumptions baked in that don't hold up on Windows.\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 10:34] Bob**: Quick search-and-replace for the separator, or something more thorough?\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 10:39] Evan**: More thorough — moving the path handling to be OS-aware instead of hardcoded, so this doesn't come back the next time we touch it.\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 10:41] Bob**: LGTM.\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 12:46] Charlie**: What about the temp directory? I remember some older code assuming a Linux-style path there too.\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 13:00] Evan**: Already on it. Fixing that in the same pass so it respects the OS-level temp location instead of guessing.\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 13:01] Alice**: How's this looking for a first test build?\\n\\n**[2026-08-10 13:03] Evan**: Once the path fix holds up under test, I should be able to produce a build artifact from it.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 36 slack thread window path handl channel releas date 2026 08 10 2026 08 1010 19 evan window build have been fail on path separ the ingest logic ha backslash assumpt bake in that don t hold up on window 2026 08 1010 34 bob quick search and replac for the separ or someth 